6526648 TREATMENTCONTROLvoiceremote_sandboxlocal_sandboxinfra_safetymemory_controlsc2sstandalone_toolboxstandalone_publiccloud_configbackground_executionsession_dashboardv3_prompttrust_classifier_shadowtrust_classifier_enforcemodel_fallback_auto_refusalevent crates/chat-cli/src/rollout.rs:292chat_cli::rolloutcrates/chat-cli/src/rollout.rsKIRO_ENABLED_FEATURESKIRO_ROLLOUT_FEATURESKIRO_LOCAL_SANDBOX_ROLLOUT_ENABLED{
652689c     "description": "Remote/cloud sandbox sessions (--cloud/--repo flags). Ramped to 100% for all users on every channel. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch (re-darkens the flags in the next release).",
65269bb     "description": "CLI LocalSandbox on V3 (the --sandbox flag, /sandbox, and local /autonomous). Generally available to all users on every channel. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch (config is compiled in, so that ships in the next release).",
6526b94     "description": "ICECAP infrastructure-safety gate (monitor/enforce). Internal-only initially; launcher exports KIRO_INFRA_SAFETY_ROLLOUT_ENABLED and the TUI advertises the capability + honors the infraSafety settings only when enabled. Ramp via treatment_percent.",
6526f3b     "description": "Persistent agent memory and the /memories command. Generally available to all users on every channel; memory starts off for external users until they opt in, and KAS's memory experiment still decides per-user eligibility.",
652707e     "description": "KAS-only /memories controls: saved memory access and automatic-update defaults, plus record browsing and deletion (list, preview, detail, delete). Generally available to all users on every channel; set treatment_percent to 0 to darken it.",
65271cc     "description": "KAS dynamic workflows and TUI workflow management. Generally available to all users on the KAS engine; opt in via chat.enableWorkflows in /settings features.",
65272cc     "description": "Cloud config: the consolidated /config panel, cloud/local source labels on config listings, and the launcher passing the stage-default cloud-config BFF endpoint to KAS for local V3 sessions. Turning this off hides the UI and stops the launcher supplying that stage default, so KAS makes no cloud-config calls unless the user explicitly sets a trusted-host CLOUD_CONFIG_ENDPOINT override (which applies regardless of the rollout). GA: ramped to 100% for ALL users on every channel; per-user activation stays governed by KAS's server-side AB_CLOUD_CONFIG entitlement, so non-entitled users see local-only sources. This flag is retained purely as the client-side kill switch: to darken the fleet, set treatment_percent to 0 in a follow-up release (config is compiled in); the immediate per-user lever is KIRO_FEATURE_CLOUD_CONFIG_ENABLED, an env override read by the KAS server (kiro-agent's feature-config provider), not by this crate.",
65276cb     "description": "Code-to-Spec Explore agent and analysis pipeline. Internal nightly only; the rollout exposes Explore and the settings control, while chat.enableC2s enables the analysis tools.",
65277f7     "description": "/tangent named side-conversations. Generally available; the launcher includes tangent in KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES and the TUI registers the /tangent command only when enabled. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch.",
6527936     "description": "Remote changelog feed fetch on stable builds (prod CloudFront). Nightly always fetches from gamma unconditionally. GA: all stable users at 100%. To darken the fleet, set treatment_percent to 0 in a follow-up release (config is compiled in); the immediate per-user lever is KIRO_NO_REMOTE_CHANGELOG.",
6527acc     "description": "Autocomplete decoupling cohort: the bundled Toolbox post-install hook asks this flag whether to move a user onto the standalone channel. It does not gate update routing, which always keeps a standalone binary on standalone archives. Ramp treatment_percent in later releases. Lowering it stops new enrollment but does not move already-migrated users back.",
6527c80     "description": "Cohort of macOS desktop app installs that switch to the standalone Kiro CLI at ~/.local/bin/kiro-cli. A desktop app release that finds no newer bundle checks this flag before it switches. Users who set standalone.autoEnroll to false do not switch, whether or not they are in the cohort, until the release feed lists 3.0.0 or later; from then every install switches. Each change to the percent ships in a release. Lowering the percent stops new switches but moves no machine back to the desktop app.",
6527ec4     "description": "Session dashboard: the /sessions browser, --sessions flag, and --resume-picker dashboard routing (v3). Generally available: every user on every channel. treatment_percent stays at 100 rather than ramping, because the single per-feature percent buckets internal users too 
6527fea  a partial percent would drop the feature for the internal cohort it was already ramped to. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch (config is compiled in, so that ships in the next release). The surface is V3-only, but --sessions selects V3 itself, so the flag is not bounded by a separate engine choice; a user who saved or passed a non-V3 engine is told the dashboard needs V3 rather than being moved onto it.",
65281d5     "description": "Who is offered the V3 ease-in prompt. Internal users ramp at internal_treatment_percent and everyone else at treatment_percent. treatment_percent 0 darkens every percentage-bucketed user, internal included; fully stopping the prompt also requires clearing v3_prompt.treatment in rollout_overrides.json. To withdraw external users while keeping internal users at internal_treatment_percent, set segment back to internal. There is no feature that flips the default engine to V3 during the ease-in 
65283fb  so a user is never defaulted onto V3 without being asked. Answers already given are honored via the persisted chat.agentEngine setting.",
6528501     "description": "Background execution for V3 sessions. One flag turns on both sides because, whenever it is on, the TUI sends backgroundExecution: { enabled: true } on session/new: the CLI display (shells chip, transcript rows for finished background processes, Ctrl+B to move a running command to the background, the Ctrl+G Shells monitor) and, from that setting, the agent's background layer itself (managed run_in_background, the move at the timeout, completion wakes, the control tool disclosed once a process runs, monitors, PTY). KAS reads no KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES; a KAS reached without the CLI is enabled by its own operator override, KIRO_FEATURE_BACKGROUND_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true. Off, CLI and agent behave exactly as before the feature existed. Dark-shipped at 0% until the telemetry layer ramps it for internal users on the nightly channel; treatment_percent is the dial and the kill switch. Opt in anywhere with KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES.",
652891b     "description": "/kvim: Neovim in a pane above the fullscreen chat. The launcher includes kvim in KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES and the TUI registers the /kvim command only when enabled. Internal users on every channel; dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch. Opt in anywhere with KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES.",
6528aa8     "description": "Permission-classifier shadow mode: on every approval prompt the engine also asks the permission-classifier model for a verdict and records it beside the human's decision, never changing the prompt. Internal nightly only. Per-user opt-out is the trust.classifier.shadow setting; the launcher exports the combined decision as KIRO_TRUST_CLASSIFIER_SHADOW; today only the V2 engine reads it (V3 is planned). Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch.",
6528cf6     "description": "Approve for me, available to opt in: the launcher exports KIRO_TRUST_CLASSIFIER_MODE=enforce (unless the user set it) and the TUI shows /permissions. The mode stays off until the user picks it in /permissions. GA: every user on every channel; the backend decides per plan who it serves, and a refused user keeps the ask prompt. This flag, and treatment_percent 0 as its kill switch, control only the mode the launcher exports; a hand-set KIRO_TRUST_CLASSIFIER_MODE is an explicit developer opt-in outside it.",
6528f59     "description": "Organization-managed settings display on V3: the /config managed category and subcommand, organization Source labels on /config, /mcp and /hooks rows, the organization-disabled/unavailable/hidden MCP row, the _kiro/governance/state subscription feeding them (off: the TUI reads only the web-tools toggle from it, as before), and the pre-session _kiro/config/template mode seed. Admin enforcement is not gated: KAS enforces governance itself. Dark-shipped at 0%; ramp internal nightly first via treatment_percent, which is also the kill switch. Opt in anywhere with KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES='[\"managed_settings\"]'.",
652924c     "description": "Re-send a turn refused on Auto, on Auto, with the refused message's reasoning envelope back in history so the backend routes the turn around the model that refused. Off, a refusal on Auto stands as the turn's answer. On for every user on every channel. The V2 engine and V1 subagents both follow the kiro-cli process's decision (KAS has its own model_fallback_auto_refusal client config). Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch.",
