66f5d6c a sequencestruct MetricSpecdescriptiondashboardattributescloudwatch_dimensionscloudwatch_client_name_dimensionstemporalitystruct AttributeSpecmetric_allowedallowed_valuescloudwatch_cardinality_hintvariant identifierP0P1P2counterhistogramlog_eventderiveddeltacumulativestruct TypesDocstruct MetricsDocmetricsMetricKindTemporality/agent/autonomous/changelog/chat/checkpoint/clear/code/config/context-gatherer/copy/custom/disconnect/editor/effort/exit/experiment/feedback/fullscreen/general-task-execution/goal/guide/help/hooks/issue/knowledge/lite/load/memories/model/paste/permissions/plan/powers/prompt/quit/reply/repo/rewind/save/session-id/sessions/settings/skill/spawn/spec/stats/steering/switch/theme/title/todos/tools/transcript/upgrade-agent/usage/verbosity/kvim/voice/workflow/workflow-run/workflowsmetrics:
66f60c9     description: Complete live diagram occurrences at their first final committed Full TUI presentation, independent of enclosing turn outcome; excludes Lite, history, discarded or pending output and failed creation without a ref.
66f62ce     description: CLI process invocations that initialized enough to identify their interface and agent engine.
66f6ae2     description: Cloud repository picker opens and submissions, with selected repository counts bucketed.
66f721b     description: LocalSandbox runtime states reported by the agent and observed by a first-party client.
66f72cc     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, os_type, sandbox_actual_status, sandbox_backend]
66f733d     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, os_type, sandbox_actual_status, sandbox_backend]
66f73ea     description: Whether a session actually ran sandboxed, counted once per session. fallback_unsandboxed is a session that requested a sandbox and ran without one, so fallback_unsandboxed divided by the whole metric is the fail-open rate and the whole metric is the sandbox adoption denominator. sandbox_fallback_reason names why a requested sandbox was not applied, including the headless config_error path that otherwise drops the sandbox silently.
66f77fb     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, os_type, sandbox_session_outcome, sandbox_fallback_reason, sandbox_backend]
66f7887     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, os_type, sandbox_session_outcome]
66f7925     description: Cloud-config sync diagnostics received in agent diagnostics pushes, grouped by severity.
66f7a93     description: Sessions that observed cloud-sourced configuration, counted once per session per surface.
66f7bf1     description: Client-observed workflow lifecycle transitions grouped by static topology and executable step count.
66f7caf     attributes: [version_full, workflow_run_event, workflow_topology, workflow_step_bucket, agent_engine]
66f7d19     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, workflow_run_event, workflow_topology, workflow_step_bucket, agent_engine]
66f7dbf     description: Client-observed terminal workflow duration grouped by outcome, topology, and executable step count.
66f7e7c     attributes: [version_full, workflow_outcome, workflow_topology, workflow_step_bucket, agent_engine]
66f7ee4     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, workflow_outcome, workflow_topology, workflow_step_bucket, agent_engine]
66f7f7e     description: Client-observed workflow node lifecycle transitions grouped by typed node kind and outcome.
66f8120     description: Client-observed terminal workflow node duration grouped by typed node kind and outcome.
66f83be     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, workflow_control_action, workflow_control_result, agent_engine]
66f85b7     description: Client-observed count of running and paused workflows after a live lifecycle transition.
66f882a     description: Explicit fullscreen preference and session-toggle changes, grouped by enabled state and bounded source.
66f89c1     description: Session dashboard visits grouped by terminal outcome, discovery path, entry point, and selected agent engine.
66f8b3a     description: Decision points of the prompts that move users to 3.0, grouped by outcome (switch, switch_failed when the launch could not be moved onto 3.0, snooze, dismiss, exit when the user quit the 3.0 launch Classic prompt, or suppressed by a prior choice) and by v3_prompt_source (ease_in for users on the 2.0 default, classic for the nudge before a Classic session, launch for the 3.0 launch prompt to existing V2 users who never pinned an engine, launch_notice for the 3.0 launch notice to users who pinned V2 themselves, where dismiss means Keep V2; a launch switch_failed means V3 could not be saved, so that launch still runs on the V3 default and the next launch asks again; the Classic nudge has no dismiss; in 3.0 launch mode a classic switch on a machine that cannot run 3.0 moves the user to 2.0, not 3.0). Records from clients that predate v3_prompt_source form a separate series without that dimension and are all ease_in, so union it in when grouping by source. A classic switch does not stop a launch that passes --agent-engine v1 from reaching the nudge again, so classic outcomes count launches, not distinct users. Suppressed fires on every eligible launch a prior snooze or dismissal silences, so deduplicate by user for reach; decision outcomes fire once per shown prompt.
66f91fd     attributes: [version_full, release_channel, os_type, install_method, distribution_type, standalone_cohort]
66f9750     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, tool_origin, builtin_tool_name, tool_outcome, execution_context, approval_path, path_scope, memory_access]
66f97e8     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, tool_origin, builtin_tool_name, tool_outcome, execution_context]
66f9b50     description: Time from prompt submission until a first-party client rendered meaningful agent output.
66f9c03     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66f9cfc     description: End-to-end duration of one logical model request, including internal transport retries.
66f9e7c     description: Time from prompt submission until the user turn reached a terminal state, by outcome.
66f9f2b     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, turn_outcome, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66f9fa9     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, turn_outcome]
66fa033     description: Launcher-observed terminal outcomes of top-level CLI process invocations, including nonzero child or command exits as failures.
66fa1fe     description: Top-level user turns whose owning process died before reporting a terminal outcome, recovered from the turn marker a later CLI start found with a dead owner, a recycled pid, or a lapsed refresh; version_full names the build that ran the turn. Reported at least once per orphan, never by two starts at the same time.
66fa475     description: How long an orphaned turn had been running when its owner was last known alive, so deaths of long tasks are separable from deaths at prompt time; same population and dimensions as kiro_cli_turn_orphaned_total.
66fa679     description: Top-level CLI process invocations ended by a signal, by which signal; the same runs count as user_interrupt in kiro_cli_run_outcome_total.
66fa833     description: Abnormal process terminations recovered from durable crash receipts or panic hooks.
66fad51     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, stall_tier, session_interface, acp_client, acp_client_name]
66fadc1     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, model, stall_tier, session_interface, acp_client]
66faf3b     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, stall_episode_end, session_interface, acp_client, acp_client_name]
66fafb2     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, model, stall_episode_end, session_interface, acp_client]
66fb130     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, retry_outcome, attempt_number_bucket, partial_output, session_interface, acp_client, acp_client_name]
66fb1ca     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, model, retry_outcome, attempt_number_bucket, partial_output, session_interface, acp_client]
66fb61e     description: Agent-layer retries of transient backend failures (throttle/5xx/network) after a backoff.
66fb6d1     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, transient_class, attempt_number_bucket, partial_output, session_interface, acp_client, acp_client_name]
66fb76d     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, model, transient_class, attempt_number_bucket, partial_output, session_interface, acp_client]
66fb872     description: Decisions on whether a turn moves to another model after the one it was using refused it or reported no capacity.
66fb93d     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, fallback_cause, fallback_outcome, session_interface, acp_client, acp_client_name]
66fb9c3     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, model, fallback_cause, fallback_outcome, session_interface, acp_client]
66fc1a2     description: Service-reported token consumption by canonical model and token category; the reported ACP client name is a dimension only in its separate name cut.
66fc293     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, model, token_type, acp_client_name, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66fc3ca     description: Service-reported credit consumption by canonical model; the reported ACP client name is a dimension only in its separate name cut.
66fc78a     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, tool_origin, builtin_tool_name, tool_outcome, execution_context, approval_path, path_scope, memory_access]
66fc822     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, tool_origin, builtin_tool_name, tool_outcome, execution_context]
66fc8c4     description: Terminal MCP server initialization outcomes; OAuth-required is intermediate and is counted only when initialization later succeeds or fails.
66fca9c     description: Estimated token footprint of raw tool specifications advertised by a successfully initialized MCP server.
66fcc30     description: Supported inbound ACP extension request attempts counted before parameter decoding, grouped in EMF by client and method. For completed-request success rate divide by kiro_cli_acp_method_outcome_total, not this counter.
66fce7f     description: Terminal outcomes of supported inbound ACP extension requests grouped in EMF by client and method. Unknown means a claimed request was abandoned without a response.
66fcf7d     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, acp_method, acp_client_name, acp_method_outcome]
66fd077     description: End-to-end dispatch duration of supported inbound ACP extension requests, split by terminal outcome.
66fd136     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_engine, acp_method, acp_client_name, acp_method_outcome]
66fd2d9     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, acp_client_name, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66fd41b     description: User turns during which at least one state-mutating built-in tool (file write, directory create, shell execution, or an applied code rename, format, pattern rewrite, or code action) ran, by terminal outcome. Built-in tools only, so edits made through MCP or custom tools do not count. Subagent sessions are excluded, and work delegated to a subagent is not attributed to the parent's turn. Carries the kiro_cli_user_turns dimension set so the two can be ratioed; agent_mode is the session's ACP mode id mapped by the same table the TUI uses.
66fd6ec     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, work_outcome]
66fd785     description: Seconds from the start of a session's first work turn to the completion of its first shell command that a local regex table classified as a test, build, lint, or typecheck, exited 0, and ran after a state-mutating built-in tool call. At most one sample per session; subagent sessions emit none, and mutations made through MCP or custom tools do not start the clock. The command text never leaves the client.
66fdcee     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, turn_failure_reason, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66fdd73     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, turn_failure_reason]
66fde99     attributes: [version_full, session_interface, agent_mode, agent_engine, memory_access, memory_auto_updates]
66fe608     description: Explicit login or credential refresh operations that ended in an unrecovered failure.
66fe713     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, auth_method, auth_flow, auth_operation, auth_failure_reason]
66fe7a5     description: One permission-classifier shadow record per stage for an approval prompt a person answered in the Kiro TUI, joined with that decision on the same tool use; cascaded siblings answered by the TUI on the person's behalf are classified but produce no record; other clients are never armed. Carries verdicts, bounded outcomes, latency and token counts as EMF properties; never command text, arguments, paths, user text, or rationale. Internal nightly only while the classifier is in shadow.
66feb09     attributes: [version_full, agent_engine, release_channel, classifier_capability, builtin_tool_name, classifier_stage, classifier_verdict, classifier_outcome, classifier_error_kind, human_decision, prompt_version, model, classifier_session_id_hash, classifier_turn_index, classifier_operation_id, classifier_latency_ms, classifier_input_tokens, classifier_output_tokens, classifier_cache_read_tokens, classifier_cache_write_tokens, classifier_request_id, classifier_status_code, classifier_stop_reason, classifier_refusal_category, classifier_credits, classifier_time_to_first_chunk_ms, classifier_user_slice_tokens, classifier_payload_truncated, classifier_dropped_tool_calls, classifier_truncated_tool_calls, classifier_truncated_user_messages, classifier_human_latency_ms, classifier_queue_position, classifier_stage2_rationale_chars]
66fee52     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, agent_engine, classifier_capability, classifier_stage, classifier_verdict, classifier_outcome, human_decision]
66fef19     description: Background-execution display events by event and cohort. gate_on/gate_off fire once per startup and are not a treatment rate; monitor_stop counts accepted single stops, monitor_stop_all confirmed stop-all requests that stopped something, move_to_background_shell accepted moves.
66ff14f     description: How long the Shells monitor stayed open per visit, per cohort, sampled when the monitor is left for another screen. A visit ended by quitting the CLI is not sampled (the process exits before the exporter can send it), so this count sits below monitor_opened by those visits.
66ff35a     description: Local V3 sessions created or loaded, counted once per session per process, by the memory access mode and automatic-updates state the agent reported.
66ff51d     description: Memory setting changes saved from /memories, one per changed setting, by requested value, scope, and whether the change landed.
66ff5f6     attributes: [version_full, memory_setting, memory_setting_value, memory_setting_scope, memory_setting_result]
66ff668     cloudwatch_dimensions: [version_full, memory_setting, memory_setting_value, memory_setting_scope, memory_setting_result]
66ff829     description: End-to-end time to load every page of the memory record list, recorded for every result including failures; the sample count by result is the load-attempt count.
66ffc52     description: Attempts to install the standalone CLI in place of a macOS desktop app install, by outcome. Queried from logs only.
66ffdb4     description: Bounded Mermaid header family; aliases normalized and unrecognized or over-budget input unknown.
66ffe26     allowed_values: [flowchart, state, er, sequence, pie, class, gantt, mindmap, git_graph, journey, timeline, unknown]
66fff71     description: Bounded raw-only presentation reason; unsupported does not assert invalid syntax. cache_evicted means local cached or pruned preview state; capacity means admission or queue limits.
6700038     allowed_values: [none, unsupported_type, width_limit, resource_limit, unsupported, display_disabled, missing, invalid_ir, unsupported_shape, renderer, timeout, capacity, cache_evicted]
6700199     description: Running CLI distribution identified from its resolved executable name; retained for EMF queries only. Unrecognized or renamed executables are unknown.
6700290     description: Standalone cutover cohort this install evaluates to. A Toolbox install reads standalone_toolbox, and any other install reads standalone_public. The value is none when the install is not in the experiment, opted_out when the user set standalone.autoEnroll=false, and unknown when the build cannot evaluate it. Retained for EMF queries only.
67005d9     description: Terminal JSON-RPC handling outcome of an inbound ACP extension request (success, client error, server fault, or unknown when no response was observed).
67007e2     description: Bounded Linux distribution derived from ID and VERSION_ID in /etc/os-release; not_applicable on non-Linux hosts.
6700864     allowed_values: [amazon_linux_2, amazon_linux_2023, amazon_linux_other, ubuntu, debian, red_hat_enterprise_linux, fedora, centos, rocky_linux, alma_linux, oracle_linux, alpine, arch_linux, opensuse, suse_linux_enterprise, azure_linux, other_linux, not_applicable, unknown]
6700bc0     allowed_values: [created, create_failed, ready, provision_failed, reattached, detached, turned_off, fell_back_local, unknown]
6700d47     allowed_values: [session_new, session_load, turn_stream, source_providers_list, source_providers_resources, list_sessions, delete_session, unknown]
6700e47     allowed_values: [throttling, auth, version_skew, not_found, network, timeout, stream_truncated, server_error, other, unknown]
670121a     description: First-party client action that changes or explicitly overrides LocalSandbox configuration.
6701286     allowed_values: [wizard_global, wizard_project, menu_save, command_on, command_off, headless_override]
67013a8     description: Isolation mechanism in force for a LocalSandbox session, as named by the agent. seatbelt is the macOS Seatbelt sandbox, bubblewrap is the Linux user-namespace sandbox, windows is the Windows container-based sandbox, and docker is a container backend. none is a session with no isolation mechanism in force. unknown is a backend the agent did not name, or named with a value this client version does not recognise; the first-party client never selects the backend itself, so it has no better value to report before the agent's first status.
6701642     description: Whether a session actually ran sandboxed, ran unsandboxed after a sandbox was requested, or ran with no sandbox requested. Counted once per session, so it is the adoption denominator and the fallback-rate numerator.
6701788     description: Why a requested sandbox was not applied; not_applicable unless sandbox_session_outcome is fallback_unsandboxed. config_error is the headless fail-open path where sandbox settings could not be resolved, backend_unavailable is a backend the agent reported unavailable, mcp_not_isolated is a sandbox the agent reported active while leaving the MCP servers an isolation policy asked to wrap exposed, user_bypass is a session a person chose to continue unsandboxed after acknowledging the sandbox was not in force, and not_applied is a requested sandbox the runtime never reported active.
67019e1     allowed_values: [config_error, backend_unavailable, mcp_not_isolated, user_bypass, not_applied, not_applicable]
6702104     allowed_values: [restored, continued, continue_failed, discovery_failed, load_failed, rejected, _other_]
67023c1     description: User decision at a prompt to move to 3.0 (switch_failed when the switch was chosen but the launch could not be moved onto 3.0; exit when the user quit the 3.0 launch Classic prompt), or suppression by a prior choice.
6702515     description: Which prompt to move to 3.0 was shown - the ease-in for users on the 2.0 default, the nudge shown before a Classic session starts, the 3.0 launch prompt for existing V2 users who never pinned an engine, or the 3.0 launch notice for users who pinned V2 themselves.
67032cf     description: Permission posture when a chat session is created or loaded; later transitions are not represented.
6703447     description: Coarse location of the resolved target of a filesystem tool, relative to the session working directory. Never carries a path.
6703671     description: Terminal state of the user turn measured by the duration histogram. A turn that ran at all records a positive sample; the host producers report whole seconds rounded up (a sub-second turn records one second) while the TUI producers report fractional seconds. A turn whose duration was not measured records no sample, so the histogram count is not a turn count.
6703835     description: Terminal state of a work turn, a user turn during which at least one state-mutating built-in tool ran. Same vocabulary and meaning as turn_outcome so work turns can be ratioed against kiro_cli_user_turns.
670395c     description: Launcher-observed terminal result of one top-level CLI process invocation; nonzero command or child exits are failures, not crash inference. user_interrupt covers every signal-ended run; the signal itself is on exit_signal.
6703aa3     description: Which signal ended a top-level CLI process; interrupt is the keyboard (Ctrl-C, Ctrl-Break) or an explicit quit, terminate is an external stop request (SIGTERM), hangup is a lost controlling terminal (SIGHUP, or a Windows console close). On Windows the report must fit inside the OS's few-second close budget, so hangup undercounts sessions closed mid-turn there and is not directly comparable to the SIGHUP count.
6703e12     allowed_values: [throttling, context_limit, timeout, connection, server_error, access_denied, invalid_request, empty_response, refusal, unknown]
6703ebc     description: Exact typed backend or service error code, limited to 64 code-safe ASCII characters; unclassified when unavailable or unsafe.
6704203     allowed_values: [completed, cancelled, iteration_limit, dispatch_failure, reinjection_failure, agent_error, unknown]
67042ec     allowed_values: [oversize, invalid_record, encoding_failure, queue_full, retry_exhausted, permanent_rejection, auth_unavailable, auth_timeout, unknown]
67043e3     allowed_values: [context_limit, timeout, model_error, tool_error, execution_limit, internal_error, unknown]
67048be     description: What blamed a model for not serving a turn, so a safety refusal stays separable from a capacity failure.
6704987     description: Whether the fallback policy found the turn another model to continue on (moved), re-sent it on the same routing tier for the backend to re-route (retried), or left the failure standing (stayed).
6704aa6     description: ACP client driving the session, so Crew (kirocrew) is isolatable within external_acp.
6704cb4     allowed_values: [authorization_denied, invalid_or_expired_credential, network, timeout, service_error, configuration, storage, identity_mismatch, unknown]
6704e1f     description: Which classifier prompt stage produced the verdict; stage 1 answers with one word, stage 2 explains first.
6704ed7     description: Parsed classifier answer; UNPARSEABLE when the reply did not follow the requested shape, and the placeholder whenever classifier_outcome is not ok (no answer arrived). Filter on classifier_outcome=ok before reading verdicts as model behavior.
6705031     description: Transport outcome of one classifier call; not_found means the classifier alias is not deployed where the request landed.
670511a     description: Bounded error class for a non-ok classifier call, limited to 64 code-safe ASCII characters; empty when the call succeeded.
67051bf     description: What the human answered on the approval prompt the classifier shadowed; interrupted when the turn was cancelled under the prompt.
6705252     allowed_values: [allow_once, allow_session, allow_user, allow_workspace, deny, interrupted, none]
67052d1     description: First 12 hex characters of the SHA-256 of the exact classifier instruction bytes, so verdicts can be grouped by prompt revision.
6705388     description: Truncated SHA-256 of the session id; joins the two stages of one action and the actions of one session without carrying the id. EMF property only.
670544c     description: 0-based index of the user turn the shadowed approval belongs to. EMF property only.
67054d3     description: Tool use id of the shadowed approval; joins stage 1 with stage 2 for the same action. EMF property only.
670556d     description: Wall-clock milliseconds of one classifier call, request start to stream end. EMF property only.
6705600     description: Input tokens the backend reported for one classifier call, -1 when no usage arrived. EMF property only.
670569c     description: Output tokens the backend reported for one classifier call, -1 when no usage arrived. EMF property only.
670573d     description: Prompt-cache read tokens the backend reported for one classifier call, -1 when no usage arrived. EMF property only.
67057ea     description: Prompt-cache write tokens the backend reported for one classifier call, -1 when no usage arrived. EMF property only.
6705890     description: Backend request id of one classifier call, from the stream error when the send failed, else from the stream metadata; limited to 64 code-safe ASCII characters, empty when neither carried one, when the one that arrived had no code-safe characters, or when the stage never ran (never_started, payload_over_budget, finalize_grace). Joins the record to the service's own logs. EMF property only.
6705a4a     description: HTTP status of a failed classifier send, read from the stream error only; -1 for every other call, successful ones included. EMF property only.
6705b0c     description: Backend stop reason of one classifier call as the streaming SDK models it; other for a value the SDK did not know, empty when the stream carried none. EMF property only.
6705bc7     allowed_values: ["", COMPACTION_REQUIRED_FOR_MODEL_HANDOFF, CONTENT_FILTERED, END_TURN, MAX_TOKENS, MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED, PAUSE_TURN, TOOL_USE, UNKNOWN, other]
6705c9a     description: Backend refusal category when the classifier call was declined, as the streaming SDK models it; other for a value the SDK did not know, empty when the decline carried no category or there was no decline (classifier_stop_reason CONTENT_FILTERED marks a decline either way). EMF property only.
6705e45     description: Credits the backend metered for one classifier call, the sum of the finite non-negative metering entries in a credit unit, at most six fractional digits; -1 when no usable metering arrived or the sum passed the plausibility ceiling of one million. EMF property only.
6705f8d     description: Milliseconds from request start to the first stream chunk of one classifier call as the transport measured it, -1 when no metrics arrived. EMF property only.
6706063     description: Approximate tokens (characters over four) of the user-role lines as the transcript rendered them (the person's words plus whatever the client or host added to those turns, any line over the per-message cap cut to it; on a record where nothing was sent classifier_truncated_user_messages can be zero while the lines were still cut); persists on records where nothing was sent, see classifier_dropped_tool_calls for the exclusion rule. EMF property only.
6706260     description: Whether the classifier saw less than the whole conversation. True when a compaction removed earlier messages, when the history was trimmed to fit (one of classifier_dropped_tool_calls, classifier_truncated_tool_calls or classifier_truncated_user_messages is non-zero), or when nothing was sent because the input was over budget (error_kind payload_over_budget). The proposed action itself is never cut.
6706452     description: Earlier tool calls left out of the classifier's transcript, either the oldest once the input budget was spent or any whose compact form still passed the per-call cap. The three trimming counts are what the history selector computed for the approval. They persist on a record where nothing was sent because the never-trimmed parts of the request (user lines, drop note, the batch's other calls, the action) passed the budget on their own (error_kind payload_over_budget) and are zero when the proposed action was over its own cap; a stage that was built but never ran or finished (error_kind never_started or finalize_grace) keeps them. Exclude payload_over_budget, never_started and finalize_grace records, and count stage 1 only, when measuring what classifiers were shown. EMF property only.
67067a7     description: Earlier tool calls the history selector rendered in compact form because the whole call passed the per-call cap (every key kept, the head of each string argument, a marker alone for a long non-string argument); persists on records where nothing was sent, see classifier_dropped_tool_calls for the exclusion rule. EMF property only.
6706931     description: User messages the history selector cut to the per-message cap, with a marker saying how much was left out; persists on records where nothing was sent, see classifier_dropped_tool_calls for the exclusion rule. EMF property only.
6706a4c     description: Milliseconds from the agent requesting the approval prompt to the human's answer (enqueue to answer). Prompts in one batch are requested together and shown one card at a time, so for classifier_queue_position N this includes the time spent on cards 0..N-1; -1 when the turn was cancelled under the prompt. EMF property only.
6706bc6     description: 0-based position of the prompt in the batch of approval prompts it was requested with. EMF property only.
6706c6d     description: Length in characters of the stage-2 explanation, so verbosity is measurable without carrying the text. EMF property only.
6706d13     description: Bounded background-execution display event in a V3 session. gate_on/gate_off once per startup; process_running once per burst of background activity; the monitor_* and move values are control-side counts, read separately from the row_* values and never summed with them.
6706e33     allowed_values: [gate_on, gate_off, process_running, row_process_finished, row_process_failed, row_process_killed, row_process_timed_out, row_process_moved, row_process_session_closed, row_process_flood, monitor_opened, monitor_stop, monitor_stop_all, move_to_background_shell, _other_]
6706f72     description: How the background-execution feature came to be on for the session (rollout, or the KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES opt-in as env), off when it was not on, unknown when it was on but the rollout list was absent or unreadable.
67070a4     description: Memory access mode the session runs with, as the agent reported it; unknown when it reported none.
6707175     description: Whether automatic memory updates are effectively on for the session (only possible with read_write access).
6707352     description: Where the change applies; access always applies to the next session, automatic updates may also reach the current session.
6707718     description: Terminal result of one attempt to install the standalone CLI in place of a desktop app install.
6707789     allowed_values: [success, bin_dir_not_writable, manifest_error, next_version_download_error, next_version_install_error]
